<p>Harry L. Hartman purchased the two main entertainment venues in the city from Rex Sanderson in early 1915: The Grand Theatre and the Rex Theater. He closed the Grand Theatre in October 1916. Hartman continued to operate the Rex Theater as construction delays pushed back the opening of the new show house, to be known at the "Palace Theatre" by two months. His Hartman Photoplay Company originally scheduled the opening of a remodeled 650-seat "Hartman House" theater for September 1, 1916, but its opening was delayed until November 17, 1916 due to construction delays. In the era where structural fires were commonplace, the construction of a "thoroughly fireproof" building at a cost of $25,000 $750,000 in 2025$)comprised of brick and concrete was a noteworthy event.</p>

