<p>A confection (i.e. candy) store was also located in the theater building. "The Palace of Sweets" sold cigars, magazines and candy, and was a very common retail store in the era. Frank Crisafulli, owner, stocked his store with "a complete stock of confections, dainties of all kinds, fruit, cigars, magazines, etc." according to the newspaper. The last movie shown, "The Ten Commandment" featuring Charleston Heston, occurred on October 27, 1957. Live events continued to be hosted at the venue through 1961. The building was eventually demolished in 1978 to become additional parking for the Wells Fargo bank. 1940 Ad Mandan Pioneer</p>
